<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Nisibis (299)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">299 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-persian-wars">Roman–Persian Wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nisibis">Nisibis</a> was the treaty of 299 CE between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> after the Roman victory over King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narseh">Narseh</a>. Rome gained territories east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> and control of key frontier cities. Accounts of the Sasanian Empire describe it as humiliating for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-ii">Shapur II</a> later reversed it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-363">Peace of 363</a>.</p></div>
